From a547e43f0faebf2ffab84d9ae685734203a362e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: coop-anything QA <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 15:21:56 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Load mod Lua files in binary mode so CRLF line endings work

In text mode the CRLF to LF conversion makes read() return fewer characters
than tellg() reported, leaving NUL bytes at the end of the buffer; Lua then
fails to parse the file. init.lua is skipped silently and ModRequire of such
a file stops the game's script processing.

Tested with an automated in-game suite: CRLF init.lua and CRLF ModRequire
fail on the v0.4.3 release DLL and on ee0e788, pass with this change; co-op
boot and independent-control tests still pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 core/src/LuaManager.cpp | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/core/src/LuaManager.cpp b/core/src/LuaManager.cpp
index 24b773c..1e97508 100644
--- a/core/src/LuaManager.cpp
+++ b/core/src/LuaManager.cpp
@@ -33,7 +33,9 @@ bool LuaManager::DoScriptFile(const std::filesystem::path &path) {
 }
 
 bool LuaManager::LoadScriptFile(const std::filesystem::path &path) {
-    std::ifstream file{path, std::ifstream::ate};
+    // Binary mode: in text mode CRLF becomes LF, so read() returns fewer characters than
+    // tellg() reported and the buffer ends in NUL bytes, which Lua rejects.
+    std::ifstream file{path, std::ios::binary | std::ios::ate};
     if (!file.is_open())
         return false;
 
